{\pard\keepn\sb720\sa120\fs34\b\cf1 The Art of Incense, Made by Hand\par}
{\pard\sl400\slmult1\sb80\sa180 At Maroma, incense making remains a hands-on craft, rooted in India's long tradition of working with natural aromatic materials.\par}
{\pard\sl400\slmult1\sb80\sa180 In our Auroville workshop, every incense stick begins with a carefully considered blend of woods, resins, herbs and flowers. These ingredients have been part of Indian rituals for generations, traditionally burned to purify spaces, accompany prayer and encourage moments of stillness.\par}
{\pard\sl400\slmult1\sb80\sa180 Today, our artisans carry this practice forward through a process of selecting, blending, shaping and drying each stick by hand. It is work that calls for patience, experience and a sensitivity to the character of each ingredient.\par}
{\pard\sl400\slmult1\sb80\sa180 Made without charcoal or phthalates, Maroma incense brings together traditional craftsmanship and a thoughtful approach to everyday living. Whether used for meditation, a quiet evening or simply to create a welcoming atmosphere, each stick carries a little of the care with which it was made.\par}
