{\pard\sb280\sa80\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf3\fs8 \par}
{\pard\keepn\sb720\sa120\fs34\b\cf1 A Little More Love for Your Heart\par}
{\pard\sb0\sa240\fs20\i\cf2 World Heart Day, 29 September\par}
{\pard\sl400\slmult1\sb80\sa180 Good food is one of life's everyday pleasures, and taking care of ourselves can begin with something as simple as a nourishing meal.\par}
{\pard\sl400\slmult1\sb80\sa180 For World Heart Day, Maroma Cafe celebrated the connection between mindful eating and personal well-being. Located on Aspiration Street in Auroville, our vegan kitchen brings together carefully selected ingredients, fresh flavours and the pleasure of food prepared with attention.\par}
{\pard\sl400\slmult1\sb80\sa180 We believe that eating well should never feel like a compromise. A satisfying meal can be colourful, comforting and full of flavour, while encouraging us to make thoughtful choices about what we eat.\par}
{\pard\sl400\slmult1\sb80\sa180 Mindful dining is also about taking time: slowing down, appreciating the ingredients and enjoying the experience of sharing a meal. Sometimes, caring for ourselves begins with being a little more present at the table.\par}
